    "https://ehwy.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3896": {
      "title": "JULIAN EUELL FUTURE FACULTY FELLOWSHIP - POLITICS",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Faculty Term - 1 Semester or Year JobSchedule: Full-time PrimaryLocation: United States The Provost Office at Ithaca College, in partnership with the Department of Politics, invites applicants for the pre-doctoral Julian Euell Future Faculty Fellowship (JEFFF) for academic year 2027-2028 who have expertise in International Relations, broadly construed. We are open with respect to substantive focus. Special consideration will be given to candidates with regional expertise in East Asia, South Asia, the Middle East, Latin America, and/or the Caribbean. Candidates trained in Comparative Politics whose research engages with international politics are also encouraged to apply. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in critical, historical, and/or ethnographic methodologies. The Provost Office at Ithaca College, in partnership with the Department of Politics, invites applicants for the pre-doctoral Julian Euell Future Faculty Fellowship (JEFFF) for academic year 2027-2028 who have expertise in International Relations, broadly construed. We are open with respect to substantive focus. Special consideration will be given to candidates with regional expertise in East Asia, South Asia, the Middle East, Latin America, and/or the Caribbean. Candidates trained in Comparative Politics whose research engages with international politics are also encouraged to apply. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in critical, historical, and/or ethnographic methodologies. The fellowship provides advanced doctoral candidates with meaningful teaching experience and mentorship as they complete their dissertations. Over the course of one year, fellows teach one course per semester, engage in scholarly forums, develop pedagogical skills, and receive professional development to prepare them for successful academic careers. The Fellowship is non-renewable. It begins on August 16, 2027 and ends on May 31, 2028. Fellows receive a $43,260 stipend, $5,000 in travel/professional development support, relocation reimbursement, office space, health benefits, access to Ithaca College and Cornell University libraries, and a dedicated faculty mentor in their program. Applicants must be enrolled in an accredited program leading to a Ph.D. degree at a U.S. institution; display evidence of a commitment to a career in teaching at the college or university level; demonstrate a dedication to equitable classroom practices; display evidence of a scholarly agenda; and be authorized to work in the United States. Candidates who have demonstrated a commitment to minoritized communities in their teaching, service and/or research are strongly encouraged to apply. Prior to August 15, 2027, applicants must be advanced to candidacy at their home institution, with an approved dissertation proposal. Preference will be given to candidates who are in the last year of dissertation writing and who will most benefit from the opportunity (i.e. those who are actively working to draft and revise their dissertation). To Apply: Interested applicants must apply and include (1): Unofficial transcript from an accredited Ph.D.- granting institution; (2) a cover letter detailing the candidates teaching pedagogy and interest in a career in teaching; description of research agenda and a timeline for finishing the dissertation; and how they will contribute to the curriculum of the chosen department; (3) a CV; (4) a syllabus for a course you propose to teach; and (5) the contact information of two references. To ensure full consideration applications should be received by November 15th, 2026. Applications will not be considered complete until all materials are in. Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. Ithaca College is committed to building a diverse academic community and encourages members of underrepresented groups to apply, and the Department of Politics strives to build an inclusive and welcoming community of individuals, with diverse talents and skills from a multitude of backgrounds, who are committed to civility, mutual respect, social justice, and the free and open exchange of ideas. Experience that contributes to the diversity of the college is appreciated. All bargaining unit faculty members shall be covered by the collective bargaining agreement between Ithaca College and Services Employees International Union, Local 200 United. Full time bargaining unit employees are all limited term faculty teaching term appointments on a full-time non-tenured and non-tenure track basis employed by Ithaca College at its Ithaca, New York campus. Information about the Union can be found here: https://www.ithaca.edu/human-resources/contingent-faculty-union . Successful candidates will be required to meet with union leadership prior to their first day. Hiring Rate: $43,260 We pride ourselves on providing our benefit-eligible employees with comprehensive benefits, including: • Healthcare including vision and dental • Generous Paid Time Off Policies • 403B Retirement Savings Plan with Matching Employer Contribution • EAP • Flexible Work Plans • Educational Benefits • Career-Enhancing Trainings • For an overview of our benefit offerings, please visit https://www.ithaca.edu/human-resources/employee-benefits-wellness In an effort to promote campus safety and the security of College resources, Ithaca College will, consistent with the requirements of the law and prudent practices, conduct criminal background investigations per College policy. This position is subject to a criminal background check. All offers of employment are contingent upon review of the criminal background check. "
    },
    "https://ehwy.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3888": {
      "title": "LECTURER - PHYSICS & ASTRONOMY",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Faculty Part-time Per-Course JobSchedule: Part-time PrimaryLocation: United States The Department of Physics & Astronomy is creating a pool of qualified part-time lecturers for possible openings in the 2026-2027 academic year to teach introductory physics courses and astronomy courses for non-majors. The Department of Physics & Astronomy is creating a pool of qualified part-time lecturers for possible openings in the 2026-2027 academic year to teach introductory physics courses and astronomy courses for non-majors. Position/Job Qualifications: Applicants are required to hold a master’s degree; college teaching experience preferred. Application review will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. Application Instructions: Interested applicants must apply online and attach a resume and cover letter. Questions about online application should be directed to the Office of Human Resources at (607) 274-8000 or humanresources@ithaca.edu . Ithaca College is committed to building a diverse academic community and encourages members of underrepresented groups to apply. Experience that contributes to the diversity of the college is appreciated. All bargaining unit faculty members shall be covered by the collective bargaining agreement between Ithaca College and Services Employees International Union, Local 200 United. Full time bargaining unit employees are all limited term faculty teaching term appointments on a full-time non-tenured and non-tenure track basis employed by Ithaca College at its Ithaca, New York campus. Information about the Union can be found here: https://www.ithaca.edu/hr/contingent_unions/ . Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. Hiring rate: $2,059.25 per credit hour. In an effort to promote campus safety and the security of College resources, Ithaca College will, consistent with the requirements of the law and prudent practices, conduct criminal background investigations per College policy. This position is subject to a criminal background check. All offers of employment are contingent upon review of the criminal background check. "
    },
    "https://ehwy.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3887": {
      "title": "CLINICAL INSTRUCTOR/ASSISTANT PROFESSOR AND ONLINE DIRECTOR OF CLINICAL EDUCATION, SPEECH-LANGUAGE PATHOLOGY",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Multi-Year Renewable Notice JobSchedule: Full-time PrimaryLocation: United States The Ithaca College School of Health Sciences & Human Performance (HSHP) invites applications for a full-time, 12-month, multi-year renewable notice (non-tenure) appointment as a Clinical Instructor/Clinical Assistant Professor of Speech-Language Pathology and Online Director of Clinical Education to begin December 1, 2026, or as soon as possible after that date. This position can be fully remote. The Ithaca College School of Health Sciences & Human Performance (HSHP) invites applications for a full-time, 12-month, multi-year renewable notice (non-tenure) appointment as a Clinical Instructor/Clinical Assistant Professor of Speech-Language Pathology and Online Director of Clinical Education to begin December 1, 2026, or as soon as possible after that date. This position can be fully remote. The successful candidate will teach assigned online classes in speech-language pathology and serve as the Online Director of Clinical Education for our online master’s in Speech-Language Pathology, participating in departmental, school, and college service; and advising students as needed. Scholarly activity is required per departmental policy for clinical faculty. The Online Director of Clinical Education will be responsible for managing all aspects of clinical placements for online students in the M.S. degree program, in cooperation with the Experiential Learning Specialist for HSHP and the graduate chair of the online modality. The position requires the ability to manage databases, maintain records, coordinate with external partners, meet deadlines, and problem-solve under tight timelines. The Online Director of Clinical Education serves as the supervisor and liaison for all practicum experiences for the online graduate modality. Ithaca College is strongly committed to increasing the diversity of its curriculum and fostering an inclusive environment for its campus community. To that end, candidates with related experience are encouraged to apply and to identify their strengths and expertise in these areas. Ithaca College continually strives to build an inclusive and welcoming community of individuals, with diverse talents and skills from a multitude of backgrounds, who are committed to civility, mutual respect, social justice, and the free and open exchange of ideas. Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in communication disorders Certificate of Clinical Competence in speech-language pathology from the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association Minimum of 3 years of experience in provision of clinical service At least 1 year of clinical supervisory experience Minimum of 2 hours continuing education in clinical supervision, per ASHA requirements Potential for excellence in teaching Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience in academic teaching in postsecondary setting Supervising clinical placements Experience and expertise in online teaching Administrative experience Experience in supporting diversity, equity, inclusion, access and belonging initiatives. Salary Range: $73,000-$81,000, commensurate with experience and rank About the SLPA Department: The Department of Speech-Language Pathology & Audiology at Ithaca College recently celebrated its 100th anniversary. The master’s degree in speech-language pathology is accredited by the Council on Academic Accreditation of the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association. Ithaca College is consistently ranked among the best in the Northeast, and is noted for hands-on preprofessional education, offering both liberal arts and professional degrees. The School of Health Sciences and Human Performance offers graduate degrees in a range of allied health and medical fields, including athletic training, exercise science, occupational and physical therapy, and physician assistant studies. About Ithaca College: Ithaca College is a comprehensive residential campus community of approximately 5,000 students, consistently ranked among the best in the Northeast. IC offers a distinct integrative learning experience designed to prepare students for the personal, professional, and global challenges of our age. Since its founding, the College has recognized the profound impact of combining academic theory with hands-on practice and a distinctive integration of performance. With 70 majors and 70 minors across five industry-leading schools, students benefit from small class sizes, personal mentorship, collaborative partnerships, and professional guidance—supported by expert faculty and first-rate facilities typically found at larger institutions. At Ithaca, faculty and staff are deeply committed to student education and growth. As thought leaders moving their fields forward, IC faculty not only mentor students but also continue to develop as professionals who use their knowledge and expertise to make a difference in the world. Ithaca College is especially noted for hands-on preprofessional education, offering both liberal arts and professional degrees. The School of Health Sciences and Human Performance offers graduate degrees in several health-related fields, including physician assistant studies, athletic training, exercise science, occupational and physical therapy, and speech-language pathology. Nestled in the heart of New York State’s scenic Finger Lakes region, Ithaca College sits atop South Hill overlooking picturesque Cayuga Lake and is just minutes away from the city center. Combining small town warmth and charm with the vibrancy of a college community, the thriving and culturally diverse city of Ithaca has been rated by Kiplinger’s as one of the top 10 places to live in the United States. Application Instructions: *Priority will be given to applications received by Friday, October 23, 2026. Interested applicants must apply online at https://www.ithaca.edu/human-resources/prospective-faculty-staff and attach a CV, cover letter detailing relevant experience and interest in the position, and the names and contact information for three professional references. Questions about the online application should be directed to the Office of Human Resources at (607) 274-8000 or humanresources@ithaca.edu. Questions about the position can be directed to Dr. Carly Jo Hosbach-Cannon, Associate Professor & Chair, at chosbachcannon@ithaca.edu. Ithaca College is committed to building a diverse academic community and encourages members of underrepresented groups to apply. Experience that contributes to the diversity of the college is appreciated. Visa sponsorship may be provided for this position. We pride ourselves on providing our benefit-eligible employees with comprehensive benefits, including: • Healthcare including vision and dental • Generous Paid Time Off Policies • 403B Retirement Savings Plan with Matching Employer Contribution • EAP • Flexible Work Plans • Educational Benefits • Career-Enhancing Trainings • For an overview of our benefit offerings, please visit https://www.ithaca.edu/human-resources/employee-benefits-wellness. In an effort to promote campus safety and the security of College resources, Ithaca College will, consistent with the requirements of the law and prudent practices, conduct criminal background investigations per College policy. This position is subject to a criminal background check. All offers of employment are contingent upon review of the criminal background check. "
    },
    "https://ehwy.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3843": {
      "title": "DIRECTOR, CLINICAL EDUCATION AND CLINICAL ASSISTANT PROFESSOR",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Faculty Non Tenure Eligible JobSchedule: Full-time PrimaryLocation: Ithaca, NY, United States The School of Health Sciences and Human Performance (HSHP) at Ithaca College invites applications for the position of Director, Clinical Education and Clinical Assistant Professor, Physician Assistant Studies. This is a full-time 12-month, multi-year renewable notice (non-tenure) position, reporting to the PA Program Director, and requires an in-person presence in Ithaca, NY. Full-time, 12-month, multi-year renewable notice (non-tenure) position to begin on or about October 1, 2026, the Director of Clinical Education (DCE) provides administrative, educational, and clinical leadership for the clinical phase of the Physician Assistant Studies program. The DCE oversees development, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of clinical education; supports clinical site and preceptor development; monitors learner performance and progression; and collaborates with faculty and staff to promote student success and compliance with applicable accreditation standards. The DCE also contributes to the didactic and clinical curriculum through teaching, assessment, advising, and clinical learning activities. Primary Responsibilities Provide administrative leadership, coordination, and guidance to faculty and staff involved in the clinical phase of the Physician Assistant Studies program. Provide clinical education oversight, including clinical curriculum, site development, learner performance monitoring, and accreditation compliance. Create, update, and evaluate syllabi, instructional objectives, and learning activities for clinical rotations and ensure alignment with program competencies, current clinical practice, and applicable ARC-PA standards. Manage clinical-phase learner assignments, assessments, progression, and remediation in collaboration with faculty, the clinical year team (CYT), and program leadership. Establish, maintain, and evaluate review clinical sites and preceptors in collaboration with clinical and didactic education team members. Develop and implement clinical rotation scheduling in collaboration with the Clinical Coordinator and clinical/didactic team. Collaborate with the Clinical Coordinator regarding clinical placement, affiliation agreements, clinical documentation, scheduling, learner records, and clinical education operations. Ensure clinical faculty and preceptors are oriented to learner assessment, program expectations, and evaluation of student achievement of clinical competencies. Schedule, organize, and conduct clinical site visits to evaluate clinical learning environments, learner experiences, preceptor support, and access to appropriate supervision. Schedule, organize, plan, and implement clinical orientation activities, learner evaluations, End-of-Rotation activities, and other clinical-year educational programming. Lead, organize, and facilitate clinical callback sessions to support integration of didactic and clinical learning, strengthen clinical reasoning and decision-making, address identified learner needs, and promote preparation for clinical practice and the PANCE. Lead and facilitate Clinical Year Team meetings, establish priorities, coordinate discussion of student performance and clinical operations, document action items, and monitor follow-through. Provide effective advising and mentoring to learners regarding clinical rotations, clinical performance, professional development, and preparation for clinical practice. Teach within the didactic and clinical curricula, including clinical cases, clinical reasoning, patient care, skills, and other content consistent with professional expertise and program needs. Collaborate with faculty, staff, the Medical Director, and other program stakeholders to integrate didactic and clinical education and address learner needs. Monitor clinical learner performance, including clinical evaluations, EOR examination performance, clinical competencies, remediation, and progression. Conduct and/or coordinate data collection and analysis related to the clinical phase and use findings to support continuous quality improvement. Facilitate clinical contract completion and coordinate with appropriate College personnel, contract specialists, and legal counsel as needed. Ensure that accurate clinical education records, including schedules, evaluations, learner documentation, immunizations, certifications, site information, and preceptor qualifications are maintained Maintain and update clinical site and rotation information to ensure accuracy in designated clinical education management and accreditation portal. Work with Clinical Coordinator to monitor that required documentation demonstrating preceptor qualifications and other clinical education requirements is accurate and up to date. Collaborate with appropriate College personnel and Clinical Coordinator regarding preceptor compensation and related documentation. Participate in learner academic and professional progression processes, including the Academic Progress, Promotion, and Remediation Committee (APPRC), as assigned. Serve as a member of the Admissions Committee and participate in applicant review and interviews. Serve as a member of the Curriculum Review Committee and contribute to curriculum review, mapping, assessment, and continuous improvement. Serve as a member of the Executive Committee and contribute to program planning, strategic priorities, operational decisions, and continuous quality improvement. Participate in faculty meetings, program assessment, accreditation activities, and other committees or initiatives as assigned by the Program Director. Collaborate with program faculty and staff to strengthen clinical education processes, policies, procedures, and performance. Perform other duties consistent with the responsibilities of the position and needs of the Physician Assistant Program. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Physician Assistant Studies, Health Professions Education, Medical Education, Health Sciences Education, Curriculum and Instruction, Educational Leadership/Administration or another closely related health professions or education discipline. If a PA, current NCCPA certification and licensure in the State of New York within six months of start date. If not a PA, current professional license/certification in the State of New York within six months of start date appropriate to the professional discipline, when applicable. Three years of professional preparation and experience appropriate to assigned clinical and instructional responsibilities. Demonstrated clinical expertise sufficient to provide clinical education and instruction. Demonstrated ability to provide clinical instruction, supervision, assessment, and learner feedback. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree Previous clinical precepting or teaching experience in an accredited Physician Assistant program, medical school, or other health professions program. Prior experience in clinical education leadership or administration. Experience developing, evaluating, or coordinating clinical education programs. Experience with clinical site and preceptor recruitment, development, evaluation, and compliance. Experience with student remediation, academic advising, and learner assessment. Experience with accreditation, continuous quality improvement, curriculum development, and assessment. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Effective leadership and collaborative skills. Competent analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities, due dates, and clinical education operations. Commitment to learner-centered education and student success. Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and a culture of care. Passion for Physician Assistant education and development of future healthcare professionals. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, clinical partners, preceptors, and healthcare professionals. PA Program Equity, Belonging, and Inclusion Statement The Ithaca College PA Program uses an equity framework to guide our work that seeks to be representative of all people including those impacted by systematic disadvantages and marginalization. Program activities and topics will enhance the capacity of our faculty, staff, and learners to communicate across differences in productive ways. The activities and topics in our program can be applied in the workplace, classroom and clinic, interpersonal relationships, and community engagement. The Ithaca College PA Program will provide a brave place for healthy discussions while respecting and caring for each other. Salary Range $116,000-$123,000, commensurate with experience. Associate Professor level considered, depending on experience. Application Instructions Interested applicants must apply online and submit a cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information for three professional references. Questions regarding the application process should be directed to the Office of Human Resources at (607) 274-8000 or humanresources@ithaca.edu . Ithaca College is committed to building a diverse academic community and encourages applications from individuals whose experiences contribute to the diversity and excellence of the College. Visa sponsorship may be provided for this position. We pride ourselves on providing our benefit-eligible employees with comprehensive benefits, including: • Healthcare including vision and dental • Generous Paid Time Off Policies • 403B Retirement Savings Plan with Matching Employer Contribution • EAP • Flexible Work Plans • Educational Benefits • Career-Enhancing Trainings • For an overview of our benefit offerings, please visit https://www.ithaca.edu/human-resources/employee-benefits-wellness. In an effort to promote campus safety and the security of College resources, Ithaca College will, consistent with the requirements of the law and prudent practices, conduct criminal background investigations per College policy. This position is subject to a criminal background check. All offers of employment are contingent upon review of the criminal background check. "
    },
