the law and prudent practices, conduct criminal background investigations per College policy. This position is subject to a criminal background check. All offers of employment are contingent upon review of the criminal background check. "
    },
    "https://ehwy.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3744": {
      "title": "CLINICAL ASSISTANT PROFESSOR AND DIRECTOR DIDACTIC EDUCATION - PHYSICIAN ASSISTANT STUDIES PROGRAM",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Multi-Year Renewable Notice JobSchedule: Full-time PrimaryLocation: United States The School of Health Sciences and Human Performance (HSHP) at Ithaca College invites applications for the position of Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor and Director of Didactic Education, Physician Assistant Studies. This is a full-time 12-month, multi-year renewable notice (non-tenure) position, reporting to the PA Program Director, and requires an in-person presence in Ithaca, NY. The Director of Didactic Education (DDE) provides strategic leadership, oversight, and continuous quality improvement for the didactic phase of the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies Program. Reporting directly to the Program Director, the DDE is responsible for ensuring the quality, integrity, implementation, assessment, and ongoing evaluation of the didactic curriculum while promoting excellence in teaching, learning, faculty development, and educational outcomes. The DDE serves as a key member of the program leadership team in implementing initiatives that strengthen educational quality, improve learner outcomes, address accreditation recommendations, and support the successful achievement and maintenance of ARC-PA accreditation standards through continuous quality improvement efforts. Working collaboratively with the Program Director, Medical Director, Director of Clinical Education, principal faculty, instructional staff, and college leadership, the DDE provides leadership in curriculum development, assessment, accreditation compliance, and learner success. Essential Duties: Didactic Curriculum Leadership Provide leadership for the planning, implementation, coordination, delivery, and continuous evaluation of the didactic curriculum. Ensure the curriculum aligns with the program mission, graduate competencies, institutional goals, and ARC-PA Standards. Coordinate course sequencing, scheduling, integration, and curricular mapping throughout the didactic phase. Promote vertical and horizontal integration of clinical medicine, biomedical sciences, behavioral sciences, clinical skills, evidence-based medicine, and professional practice. Identify curricular gaps, eliminate unnecessary redundancy, and recommend curricular revisions based on assessment findings and stakeholder feedback. Collaborate with the Director of Clinical Education to ensure continuity between the didactic and clinical phases of the curriculum. Assessment and Continuous Quality Improvement Lead implementation and ongoing evaluation of the didactic assessment plan. Analyze learning outcomes using multiple assessment measures, including: Course / Practical / PACKRAT / End of Curriculum/ Objective Structured Clinical Examinations (OSCEs); Competency / clinical readiness assessments; Course and program evaluations Utilize assessment data to identify trends and recommend curricular improvements. Coordinate annual curriculum review and continuous quality improvement initiatives. Develop reports summarizing learner outcomes and curricular effectiveness. Collaborate with faculty to implement evidence-based curricular improvements. Accreditation and Program Evaluation Collaborate with the Program Director in maintaining compliance with ARC-PA Standards. Assist with preparation of accreditation reports, annual reports, progress reports, self-studies, and site visit materials. Maintain documentation demonstrating curriculum effectiveness and continuous quality improvement. Assist in implementing and monitoring action plans developed in response to accreditation recommendations. Monitor curricular changes to ensure compliance with ARC-PA reporting requirements. Participate in ongoing program evaluation and strategic planning activities. Faculty Leadership and Development Mentor new and existing faculty regarding instructional design, teaching methodologies, assessment strategies, and learner-centered education. Coordinate faculty orientation related to curriculum delivery and educational best practices. Promote active learning, simulation-based education, and evidence-based instructional methods. Coordinate peer teaching observations and facilitate constructive feedback. Identify faculty development needs and recommend professional development opportunities. Course Oversight Review didactic course syllabi to ensure consistency with institutional and program policies. Ensure course objectives, instructional activities, and assessments are appropriately aligned. Monitor examination quality, item analysis, and alignment with NCCPA content and task areas. Collaborate with course directors to improve assessment validity and reliability. Ensure timely completion of grading, course evaluations, and required academic documentation. Learner Success and Academic Support Monitor learner academic performance throughout the didactic phase. Identify learners at risk for academic difficulty using performance indicators and assessment data. Collaborate with faculty to develop individualized remediation and academic success plans. Participate in academic advising and learner mentoring. Chair the Academic and Professional Performance Review Committee (APPRC) and other learner progression activities as assigned. Collaborate with institutional student support services to promote learner success and retention. Teaching Responsibilities Maintain an active teaching workload appropriate to expertise and program needs. Develop instructional materials utilizing evidence-based educational practices. Participate in laboratory instruction, simulation activities, clinical skills instruction, and competency assessments. Evaluate learner performance using valid, reliable, and equitable assessment methods. Program Administration Participate in admissions activities, including applicant interviews and admissions committee responsibilities. Participate in faculty meetings, institutional committees, and program governance. Assist with strategic planning and resource allocation related to didactic education. Collaborate with the Medical Director and Director of Clinical Education to ensure curricular integration and program effectiveness. Represent the program at institutional, regional, state, and national meetings as appropriate. Scholarship and Professional Development Maintain scholarly activity consistent with institutional expectations. Participate in educational research, quality improvement initiatives, and professional service. Maintain NCCPA certification, licensure, and continuing professional development. Other Duties Foster an inclusive, collaborative, and respectful learning environment. Demonstrate professionalism consistent with the Physician Assistant profession and institutional values. Perform other duties as assigned by the Program Director. Required Qualifications: Graduation from an ARC-PA-accredited Physician Assistant program. Current NCCPA certification. Eligibility for New York State licensure as a Physician Assistant within six months of start date of employment. Master's degree in Physician Assistant studies Minimum of five years of clinical practice experience. Minimum of three years of experience teaching in a graduate PA or health professions education program. Demonstrated experience in curriculum development, educational assessment, and student evaluation. Knowledge of ARC-PA Standards and accreditation processes. Excellent leadership, organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability to analyze educational data and implement continuous quality improvement initiatives. Excellent written, verbal, and presentation skills. Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and student-centered education. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in education, health professions education, healthcare administration, or a related field. Previous experience serving as a Director of Didactic Education, Academic Coordinator, Associate Program Director, or equivalent academic leadership role. Experience participating in ARC-PA accreditation reviews or self-study preparation. Experience leading curriculum redesign or competency-based education initiatives. Experience mentoring faculty and facilitating faculty development. Experience with simulation-based education and educational technologies. Experience with assessment software and educational data analytics. Strong project management and organizational skills. Ability to mentor faculty and foster collaborative working relationships. Work Environment: The Director of Didactic Education works primarily within the Physician Assistant Program and collaborates extensively with faculty, learners, administrators, clinical partners, and community stakeholders. The primary work location is the Physician Assistant Program located in the Rothschild Building on the downtown Ithaca Commons. Parking is not provided; however, the location is accessible via the TCAT bus system. Travel to the main south hill campus may be required. Work is performed primarily in an accessible indoor educational environment using computers, audiovisual equipment, simulation technologies, and standard office equipment. The incumbent may occasionally be required to transport equipment or materials between campus locations or participate in off-campus educational activities. Evening and weekend work may occasionally be required to support instructional activities, simulation events, admissions events, or other program needs. Performance Expectations The Director of Didactic Education is expected to: Provide visionary leadership for the didactic curriculum. Promote excellence in teaching, learning, and assessment. Lead continuous quality improvement initiatives that improve educational outcomes. Support successful compliance with ARC-PA Standards and accreditation requirements. Foster faculty development and collaborative program leadership. Advance learner success through data-informed educational practices. Contribute to the long-term stability, quality, and continuous improvement of the Physician Assistant Program. Salary Range $125,000-$130,000 Application Instructions Interested applicants must apply online and submit a cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information for three professional references. Questions regarding the application process should be directed to the Office of Human Resources at (607) 274-8000 or humanresources@ithaca.edu . Ithaca College is committed to building a diverse academic community and encourages applications from individuals whose experiences contribute to the diversity and excellence of the College. Visa sponsorship may be provided for this position. We pride ourselves on providing our benefit-eligible employees with comprehensive benefits, including: • Healthcare including vision and dental • Generous Paid Time Off Policies • 403B Retirement Savings Plan with Matching Employer Contribution • EAP • Flexible Work Plans • Educational Benefits • Career-Enhancing Trainings • For an overview of our benefit offerings, please visit https://www.ithaca.edu/human-resources/employee-benefits-wellness. In an effort to promote campus safety and the security of College resources, Ithaca College will, consistent with the requirements of the law and prudent practices, conduct criminal background investigations per College policy. This position is subject to a criminal background check. All offers of employment are contingent upon review of the criminal background check. "
    },
    "https://ehwy.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3740": {
      "title": "LECTURER - MANAGEMENT",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Faculty Part-time Per-Course JobSchedule: Part-time PrimaryLocation: United States The Department of Management at Ithaca College is seeking a Part-Time Lecturer to teach a graduate-level Business Analytics course in the MBA Entertainment and Media program for the 2026-27 academic year. The Department of Management at Ithaca College is seeking a Part-Time Lecturer to teach a graduate-level Business Analytics course in the MBA Entertainment and Media program for the 2026-27 academic year. This application-based course prepares students to use data-driven decision-making in the entertainment and media industry by developing analytical, quantitative, and technology skills. The successful candidate will teach topics including descriptive analytics, generative AI applications, predictive modeling, simulation, forecasting, and data visualization, while emphasizing the practical application of analytical methods to real-world business challenges. Candidates should have expertise in business analytics or a related field, strong proficiency with spreadsheet-based analysis and analytical software, and the ability to engage MBA students through applied, industry-relevant learning experiences. Professional experience in business analytics, data science, or the entertainment and media industry is highly desirable. Ithaca College is committed to building a diverse academic community and encourages members of underrepresented groups to apply. Experience that contributes to the diversity of the college is appreciated. Interested applicants must apply online at ithaca.edu/jobs and attach a resume, cover letter, and list of three professional supervisory references. Questions about online applications should be directed to the Office of Human Resources at (607) 274-8000 or humanresources@ithaca.edu Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. All bargaining unit faculty members shall be covered by the collective bargaining agreement between Ithaca College and Services Employees International Union, Local 200United. Part-time or adjunct bargaining unit employees are all part-time faculty employed by Ithaca College at its Ithaca, New York campus including but not limited to faculty in the titles of Lecturer or Adjunct. Hiring Rate: $2,059.25 per credit. In an effort to promote campus safety and the security of College resources, Ithaca College will, consistent with the requirements of the law and prudent practices, conduct criminal background investigations per College policy. This position is subject to a criminal background check. All offers of employment are contingent upon review of the criminal background check. "
    },
    "https://ehwy.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3684": {
      "title": "LECTURER - PHYSICIAN ASSISTANT PROGRAM",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Faculty Part-time Per-Course JobSchedule: Part-time PrimaryLocation: United States Physician Assistant Program/ School of Health Sciences and Human Performance Employment: Lecturer Department/School: Physician Assistant Program/ School of Health Sciences and Human Performance Employment: Lecturer Position Summary: The part-time faculty member reports directly to the Program Director. Primary responsibilities include: Work closely with the Program Director to ensure cohesiveness of the didactic curriculum by implementing curricula that is in harmony with the educational philosophy of the program. Design original or review and modify as appropriate existing curricula to correlate with program-defined goals and learning outcomes. Responsible for generating and delivering classroom learning experiences and clinical skills instruction within the basic medical and clinical science topics based on the individual’s qualifications. Responsible for student assessment and remediation in accordance with the program's remediation policy. Relative to your course, actively participate in programmatic data gathering and analysis and design and implement action plans in response to the analysis. Required Qualifications: NCAA PA certification with eligibility for a license in NYS. If not NCCPA certified, must possess a master's, doctorate, MD, or DO to meet NYSED requirements to teach at the master's level; Previous clinical precepting or teaching experience for an accredited physician assistant program or medical school is strongly preferred. Clinicians new to academia, with at least one year of clinical experience as a Physician Assistant, are encouraged to apply and will have the opportunity to work in a highly collaborative environment with active and supportive mentoring and faculty development training. Effective communicator Competent analytical skills Desire to develop as a faculty and leader in PA education. Demonstrated ability to lead, engage, and communicate with diverse students, healthcare professionals, and stakeholders. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong interpersonal skills Commitment to diversity and inclusion to ensure a culture of care Passion for physician assistant education Application Instructions Please submit CV and 3 professional references. Questions about online applications should be directed to the Office of Human Resources at humanresources@ithaca.edu . Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. All bargaining unit faculty members shall be covered by the collective bargaining agreement between Ithaca College and Services Employees International Union, Local 200United. Part-time or adjunct bargaining unit employees are all part-time faculty employed by Ithaca College at its Ithaca, New York campus including but not limited to faculty in the titles of Lecturer or Adjunct. In an effort to promote campus safety and the security of College resources, Ithaca College will, consistent with the requirements of the law and prudent practices, conduct criminal background investigations per College policy. This position is subject to a criminal background check. All offers of employment are contingent upon review of the criminal background check. PA Program Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Statement The Ithaca College PA Program has a focus on an equity framework that seeks to be representative of all people including those impacted by systemic disadvantages, and marginalization. Course topics, discussions, and activities should enhance the learner’s capacity to communicate across differences in productive ways. The skills learned in the PA Program can be applied in the clinical setting, classroom, workplace, interpersonal relationships, and community environments. The Ithaca College PA Program will provide a safe place for healthy discussions while respecting and caring for each other in the same way we would care for our patients. For additional information on the College’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion, see https://www.ithaca.edu/diversity-and-inclusion . Ithaca College is committed to building a diverse academic community and encourages members of underrepresented groups to apply. Experience that contributes to the diversity of the college is appreciated. Hiring rate: $2,059.25 per credit hour "
    },
    "https://ehwy.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3677": {
      "title": "LECTURER - PHYSICAL THERAPY",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Faculty Part-time Per-Course JobSchedule: Part-time PrimaryLocation: Ithaca, NY, United States The Department of Physical Therapy at Ithaca College invites applications for part-time lecturer positions for the academic year 2026-2027. We require a DPT degree and teaching experience. The mission of Ithaca College's Physical Therapy Program is to graduate physical therapists prepared for autonomous, interprofessional practice who provide compassionate, evidence-based, ethical, legal, and culturally sensitive care to maximize the function, health and wellness of their patients, clients, and society. Our program promotes APTA Core Values along with a commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion that prepares graduates to become life-long learners. Ithaca College is committed to building a diverse academic community and encourages members of underrepresented groups to apply. Experience that contributes to the diversity of the college is appreciated. Interested applicants must apply online and attach a resume and cover letter. Questions about online application should be directed to the Office of Human Resources at (607) 274-8000. Screening of applications will begin immediately. This position is covered by the SEIU. All bargaining unit faculty members shall be covered by the collective bargaining agreement between Ithaca College and Services Employees International Union, Local 200 United. Part-time or adjunct bargaining unit employees are all part-time faculty employed by Ithaca College at its Ithaca, New York campus, including but not limited to faculty in the titles of Lecturer or Adjunct. Information about the Union can be found here: http://www.ithaca.edu/hr/contingent_unions/. Successful candidates will be required to attend an orientation session to meet with union leadership prior to their first day. Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. Hiring rate: $2,059.25 per credit hour. In an effort to promote campus safety and the security of College resources, Ithaca College will, consistent with the requirements of the law and prudent practices, conduct criminal background investigations per College policy. This position is subject to a criminal background check. All offers of employment are contingent upon review of the criminal background check. "
